{"case_id":"C070","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":98,"change_types":["compile-time SIMD selection fix"],"affected_functions":["meshopt_decodeVertexBuffer","decodeBytesGroup"],"reason":"The commit only corrects compile-time implementation selection for WebAssembly SIMD: it disables NEON/SSE/AVX variants when SIMD_WASM is selected and prevents the scalar decodeBytesGroup implementation from being compiled solely because SIMD_WASM was omitted from its guard. It does not add or alter a public entry point, decoder protocol, initialization requirement, configuration input, or data constraint. The existing harness already invokes meshopt_decodeVertexBuffer with fuzzer-controlled encoded data and several valid strides, so no harness change is required.","evidence":["The harness already calls meshopt_decodeVertexBuffer for strides 4, 16, 24, and 32 using the supplied fuzz bytes and size.","The diff adds #undef SIMD_NEON, #undef SIMD_SSE, and #undef SIMD_AVX under defined(__wasm_simd128__), changing only compile-time variant selection.","The decodeBytesGroup guard changes from excluding SIMD_SSE/SIMD_NEON/SIMD_AVX to also excluding SIMD_WASM; its interface and decoding inputs are unchanged.","No public decoder signature, state setup, count requirement, stride constraint, or OSS-Fuzz build invocation is changed."],"recommended_action":"Keep the existing fuzz harness unchanged; treat this as an internal compile-time SIMD-selection correction."}
